I'll implement the #263 trimmed build preamble in this session: measure size on the receipt, keep the jev gate and exit contract, and add tests that fail when the full skill dump is still inlined.The build script currently sends the task prompt alone. I'll check the jev skill dump and receipt shape so the trimmed preamble stays a pointer and the size fields stay separate.The current `./pfy build -p` path sends the task prompt with no separate preamble measurement. I'll add a trimmed default, keep a full-dump flag for comparison, and record both sizes on the receipt.`./pfy build -p` now sends a trimmed preamble and records its size apart from the task prompt (#263). The working tree is dirty. Nothing was committed.

The default preamble is **87 tokens** (346 chars, chars/4). The full dump is **1164 tokens**. The ratio is about **0.07**, inside the bounds of ≤ 400 and ≤ 0.25. It still carries the jev gate (~0.85 / `PFY_JEV_CONF_GATE`) and route exits **0** = proceed/ready, **3** = escalate, **1** = broken, plus the receipt hint and a `GROK_HOME/skills/pfy-jev-decision` pointer. Skill bodies stay out of that text.

`PFY_BUILD_FULL_PREAMBLE=1` inlines `toolset-jev-brief.md` and the `pfy-jev-decision` / `jev-decision` skill bodies and keeps the real `GROK_HOME`. In trimmed mode the grok child gets `pipelines/dogfood/build/<ts>/grok-home` with only the pointer skill and a copied `auth.json`. Toolset apply still writes the configured home. The receipt `start` row has `preamble_chars`, `preamble_tokens_est`, `preamble_tokens_method` (`chars/4`), `task_prompt_chars`, `task_prompt_tokens_est`, and `preamble_mode`.

`python3 -m unittest tests.test_pfy_build_p` — 9 tests, all passed. One path ran real toolset apply, decision smoke, and route escalate (exit 3, build continued), then a fake `grok` that saw the trimmed prompt and the pointer home. `./pfy build -p --dry-run` writes those receipt fields. A nested live `grok -p` was not run. The next `./pfy build -p` without the flag uses the trimmed preamble.

